---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

---

<Layout
  title="Solar Panel Cleaning Services in Koh Chang, Thailand"
  description="Professional solar panel cleaning in Koh Chang. Remove dust, salt, and debris from photovoltaic modules to maximize energy production in Thailand's tropical climate."
>
  <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
  <nav class="breadcrumbs container" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/BreadcrumbList">
      <li itemprop="itemListElement" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/ListItem">
        <a itemprop="item" href={`/`}><span itemprop="name">Home</span></a>
        <meta itemprop="position" content="1" />
      </li>
      <li itemprop="itemListElement" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/ListItem">
        <a itemprop="item" href={`/services/`}><span itemprop="name">Services</span></a>
        <meta itemprop="position" content="2" />
      </li>
      <li itemprop="itemListElement" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/ListItem">
        <span itemprop="name">Panel Cleaning</span>
        <meta itemprop="position" content="3" />
      </li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="hero hero--service">
    <div class="hero__content container">
      <h1>Solar Panel Cleaning Services</h1>
      <p class="hero__subtitle">
        Professional cleaning of photovoltaic modules to restore lost production from dust,
        salt, pollen, and tropical debris on Koh Chang solar installations.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <a href={`/contact/`} class="btn btn--primary">Book a Cleaning Service</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Stats -->
  <section class="stats container">
    <div class="stats__grid">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-card__number">15-25%</span>
        <span class="stat-card__label">Production Recovery</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-card__number">Same Day</span>
        <span class="stat-card__label">Service Available</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-card__number">100%</span>
        <span class="stat-card__label">Safe, Non-Abrasive Methods</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="section container">
    <div class="section__content">
      <h2>Keep Your Solar Panels Performing at Peak</h2>
      <p>
        Solar panels on Koh Chang and throughout Thailand face a challenging environment.
        Coastal salt spray, red dust from dry-season winds, pollen from tropical vegetation,
        bird droppings, and monsoon residue all accumulate on photovoltaic module surfaces,
        blocking sunlight and reducing energy production. Studies consistently show that
        dirty panels lose 15% to 25% of their rated output -- and in extreme cases near
        construction sites or unpaved roads, losses can reach 40%. For a typical 5 kilowatt-peak
        residential system, this translates to 600 to 1,000 kilowatt-hours of lost annual
        generation worth 2,500 to 6,000 Thai Baht in electricity value.
      </p>
      <p>
        At Koh Chang Solar Cell, we provide professional cleaning services using methods
        specifically adapted for monocrystalline and polycrystalline solar panels installed
        in tropical conditions. Our technicians are trained to work safely on Thailand's
        common roof types -- concrete slabs, metal sheets, and ceramic tiles -- using
        fall-protection equipment and low-pressure washing systems that clean effectively
        without damaging anti-reflective coatings or frame seals. We clean both residential
        rooftop arrays and commercial ground-mounted solar installations across Trat province.
      </p>
      <p>
        Unlike general cleaning services that treat solar panels like windows, we understand
        the technical requirements. Our cleaning process addresses not just visible dirt
        but also the microscopic salt film that builds up on coastal properties and corrodes
        electrical connections over time. We inspect panels during cleaning for micro-cracks,
        hot spots, and delamination -- catching warranty-repairable issues before they cause
        permanent performance degradation. This technical inspection component distinguishes
        our service from basic pressure-washing companies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How It Works -->
  <section class="section section--alt container">
    <div class="section__content">
      <h2>How Our Panel Cleaning Process Works</h2>
      <p>
        Effective solar panel cleaning requires more than spraying water on your roof. Our
        systematic process maximizes production recovery while protecting your investment
        and ensuring technician safety on elevated installations.
      </p>
      <p>
        We begin each service with a pre-cleaning inspection and performance baseline. Using
        a clamp meter on the DC cabling and your inverter's monitoring display, we record
        current power output under existing light conditions. This measurement provides an
        objective before-and-after comparison rather than relying on visual appearance alone.
        We photograph each array section to document soiling patterns and identify any physical
        damage requiring separate repair attention.
      </p>
      <p>
        The cleaning itself uses deionized or filtered water applied through soft-bristle
        brushes and low-pressure spray wands -- never high-pressure washers that can force
        water past frame seals or delaminate cell connections. For salt-encrusted coastal
        installations common on Koh Chang, we apply a mild, biodegradable cleaning solution
        specifically formulated for photovoltaic modules that dissolves mineral deposits
        without degrading anti-reflective coatings. The cleaning sequence follows the panel
        electrical layout to avoid tracking water across junction boxes or cable entries.
      </p>
      <p>
        After washing, we squeegee excess water from panel surfaces and inspect drainage
        channels in frame extrusions where organic debris often accumulates and causes
        localized staining. For tilted rooftop arrays on Thai metal sheet roofs, we check
        that cleaning runoff drains properly without pooling on roofing materials. We then
        repeat the power output measurement under equivalent light conditions and calculate
        actual production recovery percentage.
      </p>
      <p>
        The service concludes with a detailed report showing before/after power readings,
        photographs, any damage or issues identified, and a recommended cleaning schedule
        based on your specific environment. Properties near the Koh Chang coastline typically
        benefit from quarterly cleaning due to salt accumulation, while inland locations
        with dust but minimal coastal exposure may require only bi-annual service.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why Thailand -->
  <section class="section container">
    <div class="section__content">
      <h2>Why Regular Cleaning Matters in Thailand</h2>
      <p>
        Thailand's tropical climate creates soiling challenges distinctly different from
        temperate regions where much solar maintenance research originates. Understanding
        these local factors explains why Thai solar arrays need more frequent, specialized
        cleaning than manufacturers' generic maintenance schedules suggest.
      </p>
      <p>
        The dry season, roughly November through April, brings dust storms from continental
        Asia that deposit fine particulates across the country. This "red dust" contains
        iron oxides and clay minerals that adhere to panel surfaces more tenaciously than
        organic debris, forming a thin film that reduces light transmission even when panels
        appear superficially clean. Rain during the early monsoon may rinse loose dust but
        often leaves a mineral residue that bakes onto surfaces during the hot season. Our
        cleaning process specifically addresses this baked-on layer with appropriate
        surfactants and gentle mechanical action.
      </p>
      <p>
        Coastal salt spray presents another Thailand-specific challenge intensified on
        islands like Koh Chang. Airborne salt crystallizes on panel surfaces and in frame
        crevices, creating a conductive film that can cause potential-induced degradation
        (PID) in susceptible photovoltaic modules over time. Regular cleaning removes this
        salt before it migrates into electrical connections. For properties within 500
        meters of the coastline, we recommend quarterly cleaning during the dry season
        when salt accumulation peaks without rain to provide natural rinsing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tropical vegetation produces pollen and organic matter that decomposes on panel
        surfaces, creating acidic byproducts that can etch anti-reflective coatings if
        left for extended periods. Bird droppings, common near fruit trees and in rural
        Thai settings, contain uric acid that damages module surfaces more aggressively
        than simple dust. Our cleaning service removes these biological deposits before
        they cause permanent optical degradation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Thailand's high humidity, often exceeding 80% year-round, means that dirt and salt
        films retain moisture longer than in arid climates. This persistent dampness
        accelerates frame corrosion and can promote mold or algae growth on panel edges
        in shaded installations. Regular cleaning interrupts these moisture-retention cycles
        and preserves both the optical and mechanical integrity of your solar arrays.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What You Get -->
  <section class="section section--alt container">
    <div class="section__content">
      <h2>What You Get with Our Cleaning Service</h2>
      <p>
        Our panel cleaning service includes comprehensive deliverables designed to maximize
        your solar system's financial return while minimizing your involvement. We handle
        the technical work and provide documentation that protects your warranty and tracks
        system health over time.
      </p>
      <p>
        The standard residential cleaning package covers arrays up to 10 kilowatt-peak
        (approximately 20 to 30 panels) at a flat rate of 3,500 to 5,000 Thai Baht per visit
        depending on roof accessibility and system size. Commercial installations are
        quoted individually based on array area, mounting height, and soiling severity.
        Discounted quarterly maintenance contracts are available for properties requiring
        frequent service, typically reducing per-visit costs by 20% to 30% while ensuring
        priority scheduling during peak demand periods.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each cleaning visit includes the complete technical service described above plus
        a system health inspection at no additional charge. We check DC cabling connections
        for corrosion, inspect junction box seals, verify inverter display readings against
        expected values, and note any physical damage such as micro-cracks or hot-spot
        discoloration visible to the trained eye. Issues identified are documented with
        photographs and repair recommendations, allowing you to address warranty claims
        promptly before damage progresses.
      </p>
      <p>
        You receive a written service report within 24 hours of cleaning completion.
        This report includes the before-and-after power measurements with calculated
        production recovery, photographs of any issues identified, a recommended cleaning
        schedule for your specific environment, and an updated system status summary.
        These records support warranty claims, document maintenance compliance for insurance
        purposes, and provide historical data that helps detect gradual performance trends
        indicating inverter or panel degradation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our technicians carry full liability insurance and work-safety certification for
        rooftop operations. We use appropriate fall-arrest systems on all elevated work
        and take care to protect your roof surface, garden, and property during the cleaning
        process. You do not need to be present during service, though we welcome the
        opportunity to walk through findings with you if you are available.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA Section -->
  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="cta-section__content container">
      <h2>Restore Your Lost Solar Production</h2>
      <p>
        Don't let dirt and salt steal your electricity savings. Book a professional cleaning
        service and see immediate improvement in your solar output -- backed by measured
        before-and-after data.
      </p>
      <a href={`/contact/`} class="btn btn--primary btn--large">Schedule Cleaning Now</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
